# RouteLens environment
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. `.env*` is ignored by git, with this file
# as the one exception — it documents the variables and holds no secrets.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MaxMind GeoLite2 databases
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# ASN and geography come from two local MMDB files. Nothing is downloaded at
# runtime and no address is ever sent anywhere: the lookup is a file read.
#
# Where to get them
#
#   Sign in at https://www.maxmind.com/en/geolite2/signup (free) and download
#   GeoLite2 ASN and GeoLite2 City in the MaxMind DB (.mmdb) format. The
#   downloaded archives contain the .mmdb files directly.
#
# Where to put them
#
#   Anywhere on the server that the process can read. A `data/geoip/`
#   directory in the project root is the conventional place, and `.gitignore`
#   already excludes both it and `*.mmdb` — the files are tens of megabytes,
#   they are licensed to you rather than to the repository, and MaxMind
#   republishes them on its own schedule, so they are deployment data and not
#   source.
#
#   Both variables are absolute paths. If one is unset its half of the
#   attribution is simply absent — ASN without geography, or geography without
#   ASN — and the hop table shows em dashes in the missing columns. If neither
#   is set, `/api/enrich` answers 503 and says so; the rest of the app is
#   unaffected.
#
# Keeping them current
#
#   MaxMind rebuilds GeoLite2 weekly, and a stale database misattributes
#   addresses that have since been reassigned. Re-download and replace the two
#   files on that cadence — the running process picks up a replaced file on its
#   next start, and a reader that failed to open is retried rather than
#   remembered as broken.
#
#   These two paths are read per request and are only consulted for public
#   addresses; private, loopback and link-local hops are filtered out before
#   any lookup.

MAXMIND_ASN_DB_PATH=
MAXMIND_CITY_DB_PATH=
